---
import '../../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<title>Endeavour Group — Retail Media Expansion · Kara</title>
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
		<link
			href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600&family=Instrument+Serif:ital@0;1&display=swap"
			rel="stylesheet"
		/>
	</head>
	<body class="bg-white text-neutral-900 antialiased">

		<!-- TOP NAV -->
		<nav class="max-w-[1176px] mx-auto px-8 pt-10 pb-4">
			<a href="/work" class="text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-900 transition-colors">
				← Back
			</a>
		</nav>

		<!-- HERO -->
<header class="max-w-[1176px] mx-auto px-8 pt-16 pb-20">
    <h1 class="font-['Instrument_Serif'] text-[64px] leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-black mb-10" style="max-width: 1080px;">
        Endeavour Group — Retail Media Expansion
    </h1>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-16 gap-y-4 text-neutral-900">
        <div>
            <span class="block text-sm font-medium text-neutral-500 tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-1">Case Study</span>
            <span class="block text-sm text-neutral-900">2024–2025</span>
        </div>
        <div>
            <span class="block text-sm font-medium text-neutral-500 tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-1">Role</span>
            <span class="block text-sm text-neutral-900">Lead UI Designer</span>
        </div>
        <div>
            <span class="block text-sm font-medium text-neutral-500 tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-1">Brands</span>
            <span class="block text-sm text-neutral-900">Dan Murphy's &amp; BWS</span>
        </div>
        <div>
            <span class="block text-sm font-medium text-neutral-500 tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-1">Teams</span>
            <span class="block text-sm text-neutral-900">Mixin, Criteo, Product, Engineering</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</header>

		<!-- HERO IMAGE — full bleed -->
		<div class="w-full mb-20">
	<img
		src="/case-studies/endeavour/endeavour-hero.png"
		alt="Dan Murphy's Onsite Video asset shown on desktop and mobile"
		class="w-full h-auto"
	/>
</div>

		<!-- OUTCOME -->
		<section class="max-w-[1176px] mx-auto px-8 mb-20">
			<h2 class="font-['Instrument_Serif'] text-[48px] leading-[1.05] text-black mb-4">
				Outcome
			</h2>
			<p class="text-[20px] font-light leading-[44px] text-black mb-6" style="max-width: 1176px;">
				Designed and delivered Homepage Onsite Video and Commerce Display assets for Dan Murphy's and BWS, including supplier specifications. The design system route — chosen over the vendor's out-of-the-box solution — kept the experience consistent, accessible, and on-brand.
			</p>
			<div class="flex gap-6 mt-6">
				<div style="width: 576px;">
					<p class="font-['Instrument_Serif'] text-[48px] leading-[1.1] text-black">~$13M</p>
					<p class="text-[16px] font-semibold leading-[32px] text-black mt-2">Annual revenue potential — Onsite Video</p>
				</div>
				<div style="width: 576px;">
					<p class="font-['Instrument_Serif'] text-[48px] leading-[1.1] text-black">~$3M</p>
					<p class="text-[16px] font-semibold leading-[32px] text-black mt-2">Annual revenue potential — Commerce Display</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- DILEMMA — tinted full-bleed block -->
		<div class="w-full mb-20" style="background: #F3F0EC; padding: 80px 0;">
			<div class="max-w-[1176px] mx-auto px-8">
				<h2 class="font-['Instrument_Serif'] text-[48px] leading-[1.05] text-black mb-4">
					The dilemma
				</h2>
				<div class="text-[16px] font-light leading-[36px] text-black">
					<p class="mb-0">Mixin is Endeavour Group's retail media network. In 2024, growing the network's onsite presence across Dan Murphy's and BWS was an FY25 strategic priority. The existing inventory — sponsored products, feature tiles, slim banners — wasn't enough. The exec team wanted to expand the offering fast.</p>
					<p class="mb-0">We were partnered with Criteo, who pushed for us to use their out-of-the-box ad components. On the surface it was the easier path: pre-built, supplier-friendly, vendor-supported.</p>
					<p>But the components didn't match our design system. Using them would have introduced a mismatched look and feel across both apps and both websites — Criteo's componentry sitting next to ours on the same page. The risk wasn't just visual. A jarring break in component consistency erodes brand trust, especially in retail where the page is doing real conversion work.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<!-- DECISION -->
		<section class="max-w-[1176px] mx-auto px-8 mb-20">
			<h2 class="font-['Instrument_Serif'] text-[48px] leading-[1.05] text-black mb-4">
				The decision
			</h2>
			<div class="text-[16px] font-light leading-[36px] text-black">
				<p class="mb-0">I made the call to reject Criteo's out-of-the-box solution and build the assets from our own design system instead, with the UX designer backing me.</p>
				<p class="mb-0">Criteo pushed back hard. We held the line.</p>
				<p>The reasoning was straightforward: our design system already had the components, the patterns, and the accessibility built in. Building from it meant a more cohesive experience, faster engineering (the team already knew these components), and assets that genuinely felt like part of Dan Murphy's and BWS — not bolted-on ads. It was the harder path in the short term and the right one for the customer.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- WHAT I DESIGNED -->
		<section class="max-w-[1200px] mx-auto px-8 mb-20">
			<h2 class="font-['Instrument_Serif'] text-[48px] leading-[1.05] text-black mb-4">
				What I designed
			</h2>
			<p class="text-[20px] font-light leading-[32px] text-black mb-9">
				Two assets, plus the supplier specifications.
			</p>

			<div class="flex flex-col gap-4 mb-16">
				<div>
					<h3 class="text-[24px] font-semibold leading-[44px] text-black">Homepage Onsite Video</h3>
					<div class="text-[16px] font-light leading-[32px] text-black">
						<p class="mb-0">Needed to be attractive enough for suppliers to buy and attractive for customers, while fitting the existing homepage grid. The challenge was making sponsored content feel like a curated part of the page, not an interruption.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3 class="text-[24px] font-semibold leading-[38px] text-black">Commerce Display</h3>
					<div class="text-[16px] font-light leading-[32px] text-black">
						<p class="mb-0">A feature tile sitting within product list and search results. The image needed to be responsive across breakpoints, and the supplier spec had to be tight enough that brands could provide images that worked at every size without surprises.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div>
					<h3 class="text-[24px] font-semibold leading-[44px] text-black">Supplier specifications</h3>
					<p class="text-[16px] font-light leading-[36px] text-black">
						Often overlooked but critical: if the spec is loose, you get inconsistent ads. I wrote the specs to make it easy for suppliers to provide on-brief content the first time.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- DAN MURPHY'S + BWS IMAGES — tinted full-bleed block -->
		<div class="w-full mb-20" style="background: #F3F0EC; padding: 80px 0;">
			<div class="max-w-[1176px] mx-auto px-8 flex flex-col gap-16">
				<div>
					<p class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-500 tracking-[0.2em] uppercase leading-[44px]">Dan Murphy's — Onsite Video and Commerce Display</p>
					<img
						src="/case-studies/endeavour/endeavour-danmurphys.png"
						alt="Dan Murphy's Onsite Video and Commerce Display in situ"
						class="w-full h-auto"
					/>
				</div>
				<div>
					<p class="text-sm font-medium text-neutral-500 tracking-[0.2em] uppercase leading-[44px]">BWS — Onsite Video and Commerce Display</p>
					<img
						src="/case-studies/endeavour/endeavour-bws.png"
						alt="BWS Onsite Video and Commerce Display in situ"
						class="w-full h-auto"
					/>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>

		<!-- HOW WE GOT THERE -->
		<section class="max-w-[1176px] mx-auto px-8 mb-20">
			<h2 class="font-['Instrument_Serif'] text-[48px] leading-[1.05] text-black mb-4">
				How we got there
			</h2>
			<p class="text-[20px] font-light leading-[32px] text-black mb-20">
				The path from "expand inventory" to shipped designs ran through customer research, market analysis, and stakeholder alignment.
			</p>

			<div class="flex flex-col gap-16">

				<!-- Customer interviews -->
				<div class="flex flex-col gap-9">
					<div>
						<h3 class="text-[24px] font-semibold leading-[36px] text-black mb-4">Customer interviews</h3>
						<p class="text-[16px] font-light leading-[36px] text-black" style="max-width: 1054px;">We partnered with Askable to understand how customers currently perceived ads on Dan Murphy's and BWS. The key insight: ad visibility on slim banners worked; sponsored products were often missed entirely. Engagement was about placement and relevance to purchase, not personalisation.</p>
					</div>
					<img
						src="/case-studies/endeavour/endeavour-insights.png"
						alt="Customer interview insights board"
						class="w-full h-auto shadow-lg"
					/>
				</div>

				<!-- Market scan -->
				<div class="flex flex-col gap-9">
					<div>
						<h3 class="text-[24px] font-semibold leading-[36px] text-black mb-4">Market scan</h3>
						<p class="text-[16px] font-light leading-[36px] text-black">Benchmarked sponsored product brand banner patterns across major retailers — what worked, where they failed, what we could borrow.</p>
					</div>
					<img
						src="/case-studies/endeavour/endeavour-market-scan.png"
						alt="Market scan comparing Walmart, Carrefour, Woolworths, Coles"
						class="w-full h-auto shadow-lg"
					/>
				</div>

				<!-- Stakeholder workshops -->
				<div class="flex flex-col gap-9">
					<div>
						<h3 class="text-[24px] font-semibold leading-[36px] text-black mb-4">Stakeholder workshops</h3>
						<p class="text-[16px] font-light leading-[36px] text-black" style="max-width: 1054px;">Aligned Mixin, the business, suppliers, and customers on the new inventory roadmap. Top five priorities emerged: Sponsored Homepage Banner, Homepage Video &amp; Product Carousel, Commerce Display, Sponsored products on search, Sponsored brand carousel.</p>
					</div>
					<img
						src="/case-studies/endeavour/endeavour-workshop.png"
						alt="Stakeholder workshop Miro board"
						class="w-full h-auto shadow-lg"
					/>
				</div>

			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- REFLECTIONS -->
		<section class="max-w-[1176px] mx-auto px-8 mb-20">
			<h2 class="font-['Instrument_Serif'] text-[48px] leading-[1.05] text-black mb-6">
				Reflections
			</h2>
			<div class="text-[16px] font-light leading-[36px] text-black">
				<p class="mb-0">The vendor path is almost always tempting. It's faster, pre-supported, and transfers risk. But it's also where most retail experiences start to feel like a patchwork.</p>
				<p class="mb-0">Holding the line on a design system isn't perfectionism — it's a commercial decision about how the customer experiences the brand across every screen.</p>
				<p>I'd do the same again.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- FOOTER -->
		<footer class="max-w-[1176px] mx-auto px-8 py-24 border-t border-neutral-200">
			<a href="/work" class="text-xs font-medium tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-900 transition-colors">
				← Back to all work
			</a>
		</footer>

	</body>
</html>
